<Base title="Contribute"><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Help make it better</p><h1>Contribute</h1><p class="lede">Every number should lead back to evidence. If a number or explanation looks wrong, please tell us which box you opened and what source disagrees.</p></section><section class="stack"><h2>Report a problem</h2><p>Use the public project's <strong>GitHub Issues</strong> page to report an error. The repository link will be added here when its public address is confirmed. For now, copy the box's URL and include it with your report. Tell us what you expected, what the site says, and a link or page number for a source if you have one.</p><p>If you see a person's name displayed on the website, report it as a privacy problem. Please do not repost the name in a public issue.</p><h2>Read and improve the data</h2><p>The repository's <code>README.md</code> explains the project, <code>build/README.md</code> explains the tree, <code>build/SPLITS.md</code> explains added detail, and <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code> describes how to propose a correction. The database is built from source inputs and checked before the website is exported. Some original inputs are not committed, so a full rebuild may require obtaining those files first.</p><p>There is no separate JSON download for every box. Follow a box's source references and, once the public repository URL is confirmed, its linked source files to check the work.</p><p><a href="/sources">See the sources</a> · <a href="/about">Learn the method</a> · <a href="/gaps">See what is missing</a></p></section></Base>
